# Roadmap guardrails

Phase 2 order: E14 (closed) → **E15** → E16 → E17 → E11 → E12 → E13.
Decisions below are already made. Do not contradict them, and do not anticipate a future epic unless asked.
**Maintenance:** update this file whenever an epic closes (the developer does this at epic closure).

## E15 — Domain & API Refinement

- The interactive CLI is retired; the HTTP server is the **only** entrypoint. Never create or restore CLI code,
  `Scanner` input, or TTY / `docker compose run` flows.
- `created_at` / `updated_at` (`TIMESTAMPTZ`) are **database-only**: not in entities, DTOs or API responses, and no
  persistence "model" package.
  **PENDING DECISION (do not act on it):** migration `V3` already uses a trigger (`automatic_updated_at`) and adds
  `created_by`/`updated_by`, which the epic file did not foresee (it specified explicit `updated_at = now()` in
  the repositories and no trigger). Until the developer resolves this, do not edit `V3`, do not touch
  `updated_at`/`created_by` handling in repositories, and ask before any work on audit columns.
- Every listing uses `ORDER BY created_at, id` and returns `List`.
- A paginated list plus a single-result "search" for the same resource are merged into one paginated endpoint with
  optional filters (`GET /customers/search` goes away in favor of `GET /customers?id=&email=`).
- Creation use cases return the created resource DTO (not `void`); handlers answer `201` + `Location` + body.
- DTO validation is **hand-rolled** in `application`; violations become `400` through the central exception
  handler, with violated fields listed in `message`. No new response fields.
- ISBN: only ISBN-10/ISBN-13 accepted; canonical stored form is **ISBN-13, digits only**. Validation and
  normalization live in the `Isbn` value object and apply at every entry point (body, path, query).
- Book `status` is optional on registration (default `AVAILABLE`).
- `closed_at` (nullable `TIMESTAMPTZ`) is business data and lives in the `Loan` entity.
- Book metadata lookup goes through one port (`BookMetadataProvider`) with adapters: Open Library (default and
  fallback); Google Books first only when `GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY` is set. **Never use an LLM to resolve ISBNs.**
  Never take the first search result blindly.

## E16 — Authentication & RBAC (only when it is the active epic)

Framework-free; hierarchy superAdmin → admin → supervisor/operator; Argon2id via Bouncy Castle; ES256 JWT via
`nimbus-jose-jwt` with the algorithm pinned on verification; sessions in `tb_session` checked on every request;
no hand-rolled cryptography; secrets never in the repository.

## E17 — Multi-tenancy (only when it is the active epic)

Shared schema with `tenant_id`; explicit `TenantId` value object passed as a parameter — **no `ThreadLocal` or
implicit tenant context**; cross-tenant access answers `404`; no Row Level Security; no `ON DELETE CASCADE`.

## Out of scope for the whole project

Spring/any framework, Terraform/IaC, Fargate/ALB, microservices, marketplace, payments, subscriptions,
customer-facing login, separate frontend, CORS, MFA.
